    <p>The ferry lamp swung once and steadied. Mara held the box against her coat and waited for the old man to look up. <mark>“It was not mine to open,” he said at last.</mark> The river went on talking under the boards, the way it had all night, and neither of them wanted to answer it.</p>
    <p>She set the box down between them. Whatever was inside shifted, lightly, like something turning over in its sleep.</p>
